<title>MEXICO: Mexico gives green light to Kimber-Crisoba merger.</title>
<headline>Mexico gives green light to Kimber-Crisoba merger.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Federal Competition Commission on Tuesday said Kimberly-Clark de Mexico SA (Kimber) had fulfilled the terms of its merger with Compania Industrial de San Cristobal SA (Crisoba).</p>
<p>Kimber is a subsidiary of U.S. paper company Kimberly-Clark and Crisoba was a unit of Scott Paper, which merged with Kimberly-Clark last year.</p>
<p>Kimber was forced to sell some of its assets and give up the licence to some of the products made by both firms.</p>
<p>((--Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9565))</p>
</text>
